1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,980
Hey Dex... why does Heinz

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,419
ketchup say 57 on the bottle?

3
00:00:04,439 --> 00:00:05,859
Wait, don't tell me.

4
00:00:05,879 --> 00:00:06,859
It's 57 tomatoes.

5
00:00:07,719 --> 00:00:09,304
Squished into every bottle.

6
00:00:09,324 --> 00:00:10,324
Kip... no.

7
00:00:10,964 --> 00:00:13,184
That number's basically made up.

8
00:00:13,204 --> 00:00:14,687
And it hides a trick.

9
00:00:14,707 --> 00:00:15,654
Made up?!

10
00:00:15,674 --> 00:00:17,214
In 1896,

11
00:00:17,234 --> 00:00:19,654
Henry Heinz saw an ad on a train:

12
00:00:19,674 --> 00:00:22,641
21 styles of shoes.

13
00:00:22,661 --> 00:00:23,781
He loved it.

14
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:26,221
So he gave his company a number too:

15
00:00:26,241 --> 00:00:28,272
57 varieties.

16
00:00:28,292 --> 00:00:30,828
Because he made 57 things!

17
00:00:30,848 --> 00:00:32,548
He already made more than 60.

18
00:00:33,197 --> 00:00:34,724
He rounded... down?

19
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:35,884
And nobody's totally

20
00:00:35,904 --> 00:00:38,278
sure why he picked 57.

21
00:00:38,298 --> 00:00:39,850
So it's... a vibe.

22
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:40,870
But here's the best part.

23
00:00:41,790 --> 00:00:42,390
On glass bottles,

24
00:00:43,070 --> 00:00:45,810
that 57 is where Heinz says to tap.

25
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,250
One firm tap there,

26
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:50,434
and the ketchup comes out way easier.

27
00:00:50,454 --> 00:00:51,534
I've been slapping the

28
00:00:51,554 --> 00:00:53,299
bottom my whole life.

29
00:00:53,319 --> 00:00:56,259
Okay, but seriously... why 57?

30
00:00:56,279 --> 00:00:58,059
Drop your theory in the comments.
